ng.\n40\t    - term: ticket\n41\t      technical: >-\n42\t        The X-Session-Ticket header of the reply to initialize: 32\n43\t        lowercase hexadecimal characters. A reply without it opened no\n44\t        session, whatever its status.\n45\t      observed_by: >-\n46\t        Read the X-Session-Ticket header of the last reply. It must be 32\n47\t        lowercase hexadecimal characters on a 200 reply; a missing or\n48\t        malformed ticket fails, naming the status and the header value\n49\t        the reply carried.\n50\t    - term: protocol version\n51\t      technical: >-\n52\t        The X-MCP-Protocol header of the reply to initialize, a date in\n53\t        YYYY-MM-DD form, such as 2025-06-18.\n54\t      observed_by: >-\n55\t        Read the X-MCP-Protocol header of the last reply. It must be a\n56\t        date in YYYY-MM-DD form; a missing or malformed value fails,\n57\t        naming what the reply carried.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"445fad8e-d7b6-418f-925b-12a50e31073f","uuid":"465c9f13-93d4-4764-851e-f9cf1bced244","timestamp":"2026-10-22T19:26:20.418Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/docs/architecture/architecture.yaml","content":"# Architectural spec for the `build-tests-fix-from-spec` host project.\n#\n# `build tests` reads it to resolve which suite owns a scenario: the\n# tests/<service>/ tree whose `service:` matches the scenario's. Its word\n# mapping says how each product word is built, and how a step\n# definition observes it; the step definitions follow from it.\n\narchitecture:\n  testing:\n    framework: go-test\n    commands:\n      record: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n      replay: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n      live: go test -tags bdd -json -count=1 ./tests/mcp/...\n  services:\n    - name: mcp-service\n      path: services/mcp-service\n      language: go\n  terms:\n    - term: MCP server\n      technical: >-\n        The mcp-service pr